WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.900
Next thing you know, you're in the Pine Barrens, and it hits you: your uncle's cabin.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:03.840
He has a place there.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:04.910
You're the luckiest son of a bitch.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:05.480
It wasn't luck!

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:05.940
Yes, it was.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.180
You got lucky at every turn!

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.980
I knew exactly where I was driving, I left my phone in the office on purpose,

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.560
I was in the surgical suite by design,

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.120
and I didn't use some glass award that any idiot would clearly see was missing.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.340
I made a rod out of a special dental polymer,

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.260
killed him with it, then melted it back down.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.880
It's already in a patient's mouth.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:22.480
son!

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.220
of a bitch.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:28.940
Oh, damn.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.320
Oh, damn.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.620
Oh, damn!

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.540
And that is three oh damns.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.300
Oh, damn!

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:37.520
Ohhh.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.340
Fresh air.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.880
Wow, I don't say that a lot.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.640
There's one thing I still don't understand.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.040
Did you know you had the wrong murder weapon?

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.800
Ah, excellent question, sir.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:52.180
Yes.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.020
I spotted the missing dental award when I first took the case.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.360
I asked around weeks ago.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:58.580
Turns out a cleaning lady knocked it over and shattered it.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.010
Then why did you run in there like that?

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:03.220
Because in talking to you, I realized what Philip's worst fear actually was:

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:05.580
that we would think he was just some dummy that got lucky.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.480
Right.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.480
He had planned the perfect crime.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.260
And it killed him when you said he was sloppy and impulsive.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:12.840
He needed us to know how smart he was.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:13.240
Right.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:15.180
Like someone else I know.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:16.260
Yup.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:17.700
Kevin.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.180
I'm proud of you, Peralta.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.220
Thank you, sir.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.120
Now let's go get some sleep.
